# Summary of Findings

| Security Control          | Initial State       | Action                            | Final State |
| ------------------------- | ------------------- | --------------------------------- | ----------- |
| Windows Firewall          | Disabled            | Enabled                           | Hardened    |
| Inbound firewall behavior | Unprotected         | Default blocking applied          | Hardened    |
| Microsoft Defender        | Protections enabled | No change required                | Secure      |
| UAC                       | Appropriate         | No change required                | Secure      |
| Administrator privileges  | Reviewed            | No unnecessary members identified | Reviewed    |
| Password length           | 0                   | Increased to 12                   | Hardened    |
| Password complexity       | Disabled            | Enabled                           | Hardened    |
| Password history          | 0                   | Increased to 5                    | Hardened    |

# Security Recommendations

Based on the assessment:

1. Keep Windows Firewall enabled across all network profiles.
2. Maintain Microsoft Defender protections and Tamper Protection.
3. Keep UAC enabled.
4. Regularly review local administrator memberships.
5. Enforce strong password requirements.
6. Maintain appropriate password history controls.
7. Regularly apply Windows security updates.
8. Review Windows security logs for suspicious activity.
9. Periodically reassess endpoint security configurations.

# Conclusion

This lab provided hands-on experience assessing and hardening a Windows endpoint.

The assessment identified several security controls that were already appropriately configured, as well as weaknesses in the Windows Firewall and password policy.

The firewall was enabled and configured to block unsolicited inbound connections, while the password policy was strengthened through increased minimum password length, password complexity requirements, and password history.

The exercise demonstrates the importance of establishing a security baseline, identifying weaknesses, applying targeted remediation, and verifying the resulting configuration.

## Disclaimer

This assessment was conducted exclusively on an authorized Windows virtual machine within an isolated personal cybersecurity laboratory. No unauthorized systems or networks were targeted.
